{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Algebra","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.AdjoinRoot"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.rankOneModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.rankOneModel","kind":"instance","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L133-L146","doc":"**The class admits a rank-1 model at every `n`.** `ℚ` itself is a\n`HeckeAlgebra ℚ n 1 ℚ` for all `n` — including `n` where `H_n(1)` has\ndimension `n! = 6, 24, 120, …`.\n\nSo a hypothesis `[HeckeAlgebra R n q A]` is much weaker than \"`A` is the\nHecke algebra\": anything proved from it also holds of `ℚ` at `q = 1`. The\nmissing axiom is the **Iwahori basis** — `A` free of rank `n!` over `R` on\n`{T_w}_{w ∈ S_n}`. See bean qou-ghak / the H3–H4 roadmap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.instHeckeAlgebraH2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.instHeckeAlgebraH2","kind":"instance","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L104-L120","doc":"**`H₂(q)` is a Hecke algebra.** All four axioms discharged: the quadratic\nrelation from the defining polynomial, braid and far-commutativity\nvacuously (one generator), and spanning from `AdjoinRoot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.not_farCommuting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.not_farCommuting","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L95-L102","doc":"…and none are ever far-commuting either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.not_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.not_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L88-L93","doc":"`Generator 2` has a single index, so no two generators are ever adjacent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.sigma_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.sigma_sq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The defining relation, in the form the Hecke class wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.aeval_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.aeval_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L71-L79","doc":"The quadratic relation, stated over an abstract carrier so that no\nunfolding of the `AdjoinRoot` *type* is ever needed — that is what made the\ndirect proof fight `rw`'s motive check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.sigma","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L68-L69","doc":"The generator `σ₁ ∈ H₂(q)`, the image of `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.H2","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L60-L66","doc":"**The two-strand Hecke algebra** `H₂(q) = R[X]/(X² − (q − q⁻¹)X − 1)`.\n\n`abbrev`, not `def`: the `AdjoinRoot` ring and algebra instances must stay\nvisible to instance search, and the type must be reducibly equal to\n`AdjoinRoot (heckePoly R q)` so `algebraMap R (H2 R q)` elaborates to the\nsame term the `AdjoinRoot` lemmas produce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.heckePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.heckePoly","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The defining polynomial `X² − h·X − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.heckeParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.heckeParam","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/InstanceH2.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹` of the §7a convention. ","signatureChunk":0}]}